      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That feeling of a core foundation crumbling is devastating, and it makes perfect sense that you feel lost when twenty years of self-definition are suddenly gone. When the familiar self feels inadequate, it's a deeply disorienting crisis. Instead of trying to instantly build a \"new\" self, perhaps focus on small acts of rediscovery, noticing what brings even a sliver of comfort or curiosity outside of the research. These small anchors can start to rebuild a sense of self-worth gradually.",
      "source": "target",
